WEBVTT

00:01.230 --> 00:03.730
Previously on Captain Tsubasa.

00:03.730 --> 00:05.810
Tsubasa and the others train,

00:05.810 --> 00:08.820
for their match against Wakabayashi, their rival.

00:08.820 --> 00:10.280
Each one of them have followed the individual practise,

00:10.280 --> 00:13.570
and they are getting day by day.

00:13.570 --> 00:19.790
Wakabayashi was also practising vigorously for the match.

00:20.790 --> 00:24.790
I'm looking forward to the match, Oozora Tsubasa.

00:24.790 --> 00:31.260
And again, by fate, a young boy arrives in Nankatsu town.

00:32.170 --> 00:34.220
He's good at dribbling.

00:34.220 --> 00:37.930
Everybody's here and the time has come.

00:37.930 --> 00:40.430
The showdown between Tsubasa and Wakabayashi,

00:40.430 --> 00:44.060
is about to begin.

00:56.070 --> 01:01.700
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

00:56.070 --> 01:01.700
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:01.700 --> 01:06.830
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:01.700 --> 01:06.830
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:07.460 --> 01:12.960
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:07.460 --> 01:12.960
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:12.960 --> 01:20.890
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:12.960 --> 01:20.890
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:20.890 --> 01:26.640
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:20.890 --> 01:26.640
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:26.640 --> 01:35.150
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:26.640 --> 01:35.150
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:35.150 --> 01:40.950
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:35.320 --> 01:40.950
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:40.950 --> 01:46.870
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:40.950 --> 01:46.870
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

01:46.870 --> 01:48.500
<i>Run & Run!</i>

01:48.500 --> 01:55.800
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

01:48.500 --> 01:55.800
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

01:55.800 --> 01:58.720
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

01:55.800 --> 01:58.720
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

01:58.720 --> 02:03.640
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

01:58.720 --> 02:03.640
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:14.280 --> 02:17.950
<b><b>Episode 6: KICK-OFF!
NANKATSU vs. SHUUTETSU
</b></b>

02:18.570 --> 02:22.370
<b><b>- 22nd of April, Private Shuutetsu Elementary School -</b></b>

02:22.370 --> 02:26.130
Sign: 26th Shuutetsu Elementary-Nankatsu Elementary
Inter-school Tournament

02:22.370 --> 02:25.410
Nankatsu Elementary vs. Shuutetsu Elementary,

02:25.410 --> 02:26.250
begins.

02:26.910 --> 02:28.670
One point and the match is over.

02:29.420 --> 02:35.590
It wasn't long before fierce competition
starts between the two schools

02:35.590 --> 02:38.590
putting their name on the line and in the middle of chants.

02:38.590 --> 02:43.100
Hooray... Hooray... Nankatsu!

02:44.100 --> 02:44.970
Strike!

02:44.970 --> 02:46.350
Oh...

02:46.350 --> 02:49.060
Hey, you know what happened to the Boss?

02:49.060 --> 02:52.980
I don't know. What is she doing at an important time like this?

02:52.980 --> 02:55.650
Forget about that, and cheer harder!

02:55.650 --> 02:56.530
Yes, sir!

02:56.530 --> 02:58.360
Let's go to the court this time.

02:58.360 --> 03:02.450
This year's Nankatsu Basketball Club is in good form.

03:05.870 --> 03:08.000
Oh, the football club.

03:08.000 --> 03:10.290
Yes, we have arrived.

03:10.290 --> 03:12.880
What were you doing up until now,

03:12.880 --> 03:14.130
not showing up at the opening ceremony?

03:15.210 --> 03:17.840
We were doing last minute practise,

03:17.840 --> 03:21.220
and had a strategy meeting. Right, Tsubasa?

03:21.220 --> 03:21.800
Yes.

03:22.720 --> 03:24.300
It's time for the match.

03:24.300 --> 03:28.560
I'll be able to challenge Wakabayashi in a match.

03:31.560 --> 03:34.360
Okay, this time's program...

03:35.110 --> 03:37.650
has football at the last.

03:37.650 --> 03:40.110
We have time until then,

03:40.110 --> 03:42.110
so let's go and see the other clubs' matches.

03:42.110 --> 03:42.860
Sure.

03:42.860 --> 03:46.490
We need to win the inter-school tournament
before it comes to that point then.

03:46.490 --> 03:48.240
What did you say, prick?

03:48.240 --> 03:51.460
You're underestimating the football club, aren't you?

03:51.460 --> 03:52.750
No, we're not.

03:57.000 --> 04:00.300
This is gonna be our little castle for now.

04:02.260 --> 04:03.300
Wow.

04:06.470 --> 04:10.060
Dad, the scenery is nice from here.

04:15.100 --> 04:16.980
I'm going out, Tarou.

04:16.980 --> 04:17.980
Okay.

04:21.320 --> 04:23.150
Okay, let's go.

04:33.120 --> 04:34.540
Roberto?

04:36.290 --> 04:37.840
Mrs. Oozora!

04:37.840 --> 04:40.090
What're you doing here?

04:40.090 --> 04:43.880
There's a lot of time till the match starts.

04:43.880 --> 04:46.760
No, I'm just daydreaming here.

04:47.430 --> 04:51.180
If I'm looking at the empty field here,

04:51.180 --> 04:56.730
the infinite amount plays that Tsubasa
may show me comes into my mind.

04:58.060 --> 05:02.400
I was surprised practising with Tsubasa for two weeks.

05:02.400 --> 05:06.200
He's just like me in a different body.

05:07.070 --> 05:13.620
If I shout "move like this, aim there" in my mind,

05:13.620 --> 05:18.250
he moves there as if he reads my mind and shoots the ball.

05:20.040 --> 05:23.510
Pretty sure I'm gonna feel like I'm playing,

05:23.510 --> 05:26.720
when I see Tsubasa play.

05:30.470 --> 05:34.560
I feel you can take Tsubasa to the world.

05:34.560 --> 05:35.310
What?

05:35.310 --> 05:37.650
Tsubasa always says,

05:37.650 --> 05:41.070
that he wants to make Japanese football the best in the world.

05:41.070 --> 05:44.070
That's a big dream.

05:44.070 --> 05:47.200
And that's a dream worth challenging.

05:52.200 --> 05:58.920
Let's make that dream come true together
one day, shouldn't we Tsubasa?

05:58.920 --> 06:03.090
Now, we will begin the Boy's 200-meter run.

06:03.090 --> 06:05.590
Huh, 6th row is empty.

06:05.590 --> 06:09.640
Our participant got injured and withdrew.

06:10.720 --> 06:14.470
That being said, this year's line-up is really bad.

06:14.470 --> 06:17.350
If you look, Shuutetsu's gotten all the first places.

06:17.350 --> 06:18.850
What did you say?

06:18.850 --> 06:21.810
Do you think you guys can say such cocky things?

06:21.810 --> 06:22.940
What?

06:22.940 --> 06:25.650
You guys always lose.

06:25.650 --> 06:29.240
You guys lost 30-0 to Shuutetsu.

06:29.240 --> 06:30.410
On your marks.

06:30.410 --> 06:32.780
Shuutetsu has Wakabayashi,

06:32.780 --> 06:34.490
who won without giving a single goal.

06:34.490 --> 06:37.160
You guys can't even score a goal. Haha.

06:38.160 --> 06:38.920
Ready?

06:40.460 --> 06:42.290
You wanna do it, you bastard?

06:42.290 --> 06:43.670
Wait, Ishizaki...

06:44.630 --> 06:45.710
look there.

06:45.710 --> 06:46.460
What?

06:47.220 --> 06:48.550
The heck?!

06:51.680 --> 06:52.720
Alright.

06:52.720 --> 06:54.350
Tsubasa!

06:55.140 --> 06:59.690
Ah, what is he doing? Who is he?

06:59.690 --> 07:04.070
Suddenly, a kid dribbling with his football just came into the track.

07:06.940 --> 07:08.530
That's impossible!

07:08.530 --> 07:11.740
How come he's faster than the normally running people?

07:11.740 --> 07:16.240
Here he comes! The mysterious dribbling kid has caught up!

07:20.250 --> 07:21.880
Woah!

07:21.880 --> 07:25.500
He's run past all of and took the lead in an instant.

07:25.500 --> 07:27.380
Awesome, Tsubasa!

07:27.380 --> 07:31.380
What a cornering by the mysterious dribbling kid!

07:31.380 --> 07:33.890
He isn't losing any speed.

07:34.100 --> 07:35.720
What is he?

07:35.720 --> 07:36.810
Impossible!

07:37.930 --> 07:40.690
Here, he's into the last part of the race!

07:40.690 --> 07:43.520
Alright, time for the last sprint.

07:43.520 --> 07:46.900
Look at that, the mysterious dribbling kid
speeds up here. Incredible!

07:46.900 --> 07:50.990
Will he be able to continue pulling himself away just like this?

07:50.990 --> 07:53.740
Also, what's with that look on your face, tracking club?

07:53.740 --> 07:54.570
Go!

07:54.570 --> 07:55.450
Tsubasa!

07:55.450 --> 07:56.530
Big!

07:56.530 --> 07:59.910
Do it, Tsubasa!

08:08.090 --> 08:09.630
I did it!

08:09.630 --> 08:14.720
GOAL! The winner of the first race is
the mystery dribbling kid at 6th row!

08:14.720 --> 08:15.600
Yes!

08:15.600 --> 08:16.850
No way!

08:16.850 --> 08:19.520
I mean, really?

08:41.040 --> 08:43.120
Alright, the composition is done.

08:44.500 --> 08:47.540
Then, I'll go get my school work done.

08:47.540 --> 08:50.340
It's Nankatsu Elementary this time, right?

08:59.890 --> 09:02.810
Ah, Matsuyama!

09:00.850 --> 09:04.100
Inbox: Matsuyama (from Furano Elementary)

09:04.100 --> 09:07.020
<b><b>- Shuutetsu Elementary football stadium -</b></b>

09:11.960 --> 09:16.910
<b><b>- Yamabuki Elementary football club -</b></b>

09:12.360 --> 09:16.910
Listen carefully, collect data on Shuutetsu properly today.

09:16.910 --> 09:22.080
If we don't beat Shuutetsu, we can't go to the nationals.

09:22.080 --> 09:23.330
Shuutetsu!

09:25.460 --> 09:29.040
But, will the important guy Wakabayashi play...

09:29.040 --> 09:30.550
Wakabayashi will play!

09:30.550 --> 09:31.210
What?

09:32.050 --> 09:35.380
You're... Nishigaoka Elementary's Urabe!

09:35.380 --> 09:40.970
Unlike you guys, we came to see Wakabayashi let in goals against them.

09:40.970 --> 09:44.140
Shuutetsu might lose this match.

09:44.140 --> 09:46.020
What?

09:46.020 --> 09:49.980
Woah... So it happens.

09:49.980 --> 09:53.530
Nankatsu vs. Shuutetsu, it's still a draw.

09:53.530 --> 09:59.450
That means, this year's result will
be decided by the football match!!

09:59.450 --> 10:01.830
This is getting interesting!

10:01.830 --> 10:06.500
Everbody, we'll put everything we have and cheer for them.

10:06.500 --> 10:07.670
Yes, sir!

10:10.840 --> 10:12.000
Eh!

10:12.000 --> 10:14.340
Are you a transfer student?

10:14.340 --> 10:18.130
Everybody's gone to Shuutetsu Elementary.

10:18.130 --> 10:19.510
Shuutetsu Elementary?

10:35.940 --> 10:38.030
Today's the day, eh?

10:38.030 --> 10:39.200
Yep.

10:39.200 --> 10:41.370
The day I met you,

10:41.370 --> 10:45.700
is when Wakabayashi said he would accept your challenge through a match.

10:45.700 --> 10:48.790
Everything started on that day.

10:48.790 --> 10:50.460
What happened, suddenly?

10:50.460 --> 10:52.540
Trying to act cool?

10:52.540 --> 10:54.630
Yep, trying to be cool.

10:54.630 --> 10:55.420
Eh!

10:56.210 --> 11:00.930
It's a bit of an exaggeration, but I'm glad I met you.

11:00.930 --> 11:03.510
I'm firing up for a football match,

11:03.510 --> 11:05.390
for the first time in my life.

11:05.390 --> 11:08.600
Let's have a good match, Ishizaki.

11:08.600 --> 11:10.440
Everybody, I am counting on you today.

11:10.440 --> 11:12.900
Yes.

11:12.900 --> 11:15.070
Not just a good match, let's win!

11:15.070 --> 11:16.690
You said it!

11:16.690 --> 11:19.990
Just tried to be cool, like somebody.

11:22.200 --> 11:24.740
Let's go, everyone!

11:24.740 --> 11:26.240
Sure!

11:45.430 --> 11:46.560
Woah!

11:46.560 --> 11:47.810
Eh!

11:48.730 --> 11:51.980
We're with you, Nankatsu Eleven!

11:52.650 --> 11:54.440
Really, there's that much people?

11:54.440 --> 11:56.860
Ah, my leg's started to shake!

11:56.860 --> 12:01.910
I'm gonna play a match in front of all those people.

12:01.910 --> 12:04.240
You're here, everyone.

12:04.240 --> 12:05.580
Roberto!

12:05.580 --> 12:06.950
What's with you guys?

12:06.950 --> 12:10.460
The more people present, the better to play.

12:10.460 --> 12:12.330
But...

12:12.330 --> 12:14.880
Tsubasa, when you reach to the world,

12:14.880 --> 12:16.840
the atmosphere is not even comparable to this.

12:23.760 --> 12:24.300
Uh!

12:24.970 --> 12:27.890
They're used it, huh?

12:27.890 --> 12:31.020
We're scared to death here...

12:31.020 --> 12:32.520
Wakabayashi's not here.

12:32.520 --> 12:33.140
Eh!

12:47.780 --> 12:48.990
It's no good, Coach.

12:48.990 --> 12:51.410
We can't find our captain anywhere.

12:51.410 --> 12:53.000
Is that so?

12:53.000 --> 12:54.210
It can't be helped.

12:54.210 --> 12:56.040
We'll go without Wakabayashi today.

12:56.040 --> 12:58.460
I believe we don't need to worry
because our opponent is Nankatsu,

12:58.460 --> 13:00.210
but still, play with care today.

13:00.210 --> 13:01.590
Yeah!

13:01.590 --> 13:03.590
Next in the inter-school tournament is

13:03.590 --> 13:07.760
Shuutetsu Elementary Football Club vs. Nankatsu Elementary Football Club.

13:13.060 --> 13:15.190
Why do I have to go all the way to Shuutetsu Elementary

13:15.190 --> 13:18.860
to have myself enrolled in Nankatsu Elementary?

13:18.860 --> 13:19.610
All right!

13:19.610 --> 13:21.150
I'll send the ball through that gap next to the pole

13:21.150 --> 13:22.740
make the shot hit the wall!

13:25.990 --> 13:26.950
Watch out!

13:30.030 --> 13:33.910
You shouldn't recklessly
kick the ball around in town like that.

13:35.960 --> 13:37.880
Are you serious? Hasn't Wakabayashi come?

13:37.880 --> 13:40.000
Yes, this might be our chance.

13:40.000 --> 13:41.880
If that prodigy goalkeeper isn't here,

13:41.880 --> 13:43.760
we can hope to win.

13:43.760 --> 13:47.220
Our football club has been working hard lately.

13:47.220 --> 13:48.390
I've seen them.

13:48.390 --> 13:50.180
They were dribbling all the time.

13:50.180 --> 13:52.020
That lame football club becoming like that...

13:53.890 --> 13:55.180
You heard that?

13:55.180 --> 13:58.860
Who was the one saying that
Wakabayashi would definitely come again?

14:00.320 --> 14:02.780
This isn't supposed to happen.

14:05.530 --> 14:08.160
I wonder what happened to Wakabayashi.

14:08.160 --> 14:11.200
Maybe he was so afraid of you that he ran.

14:11.200 --> 14:13.490
Hey Ishizaki, your jokes are sure harsh.

14:14.120 --> 14:15.790
Wakabayashi!

14:19.540 --> 14:22.210
Coach, our captain has come.

14:24.960 --> 14:27.470
What's with you?

14:27.470 --> 14:30.550
Oozora Tsubasa, like I told you before,

14:30.550 --> 14:33.010
this match will be a challenge to see

14:33.010 --> 14:36.180
whether you can score a goal against me.

14:36.180 --> 14:38.270
I won't score just one goal.

14:38.270 --> 14:41.190
Nankatsu will beat Shuutetsu in this match.

15:01.880 --> 15:04.750
Nankatsu Elementary's principal is here, I guess.

15:04.750 --> 15:08.510
Oh, you are dribbling just like Tsubasa!

15:09.590 --> 15:10.680
Tsubasa?

15:10.680 --> 15:12.010
Yes, Tsubasa.

15:12.010 --> 15:14.350
Do you play football, too?

15:14.350 --> 15:17.270
But you see, our Tsubasa is really great.

15:18.140 --> 15:19.390
Come with me.

15:19.390 --> 15:20.940
I'm going to cheer him on.

15:20.940 --> 15:22.230
Wait a second.

15:22.230 --> 15:23.900
I need to find Nankatsu's...

15:23.900 --> 15:27.740
Come on already, I'm the leader of the
Nankatsu Elementary cheering squad.

15:27.740 --> 15:30.910
Fight... Fight... Shuutetsu!

15:30.910 --> 15:33.780
Boss didn't come in the end.

15:33.780 --> 15:36.660
Whew, I've made it on time.

15:36.660 --> 15:38.040
Boss!

15:39.500 --> 15:40.710
Look at him.

15:40.710 --> 15:42.710
That's Tsubasa.

15:42.710 --> 15:43.710
Ah...

15:47.880 --> 15:49.260
It's that guy.

15:49.260 --> 15:51.130
Hey you...

15:52.470 --> 15:54.140
Why are you with our Boss?

15:54.800 --> 15:56.890
I just met her over there.

15:56.890 --> 16:00.060
I'm transferring to Nankatsu Elementary today.

16:00.060 --> 16:01.480
What? Transferring?

16:01.480 --> 16:04.650
My name is Misaki Tarou. Nice to meet you.

16:06.190 --> 16:10.110
Hooray... Hooray... Tsubasa!

16:10.110 --> 16:14.240
Fight.. Fight.. Tsubasa!

16:14.240 --> 16:17.080
[on flag: Fight Tsubasa]

16:15.120 --> 16:17.080
Boss...

16:17.080 --> 16:18.240
There she goes again...

16:18.240 --> 16:19.250
This is so cool.

16:19.250 --> 16:20.910
It only has Tsubasa's name on it.

16:20.910 --> 16:24.170
Being popular must be hard, Tsubasa.

16:24.170 --> 16:27.300
Tsubasa! Do your best!

16:29.960 --> 16:31.800
I'm sorry that I'm late.

16:31.800 --> 16:32.970
So you have come.

16:32.970 --> 16:34.090
Yes.

16:34.090 --> 16:35.930
I'm counting on you, Captain.

16:35.930 --> 16:36.550
Yes.

16:38.850 --> 16:40.180
Listen to me, guys!

16:40.180 --> 16:43.100
Whatever happens, just don't let Oozora Tsubasa

16:43.100 --> 16:46.650
score a goal in this match.

16:46.650 --> 16:48.570
After all, this match is a contest between us

16:48.570 --> 16:52.030
to see if he can score a goal against me.

16:52.030 --> 16:53.240
- Shimada.
- Yes!

16:53.240 --> 16:54.450
- Nakamoto.
- Yes!

16:54.450 --> 16:56.620
Just leave the other small fry alone.

16:56.620 --> 16:59.740
You two will constantly mark
Oozora Tsubasa when he attacks.

16:59.740 --> 17:00.200
Yes.

17:00.200 --> 17:01.410
Understood.

17:01.410 --> 17:05.500
It's enough if you just mark him in the penalty area.

17:05.500 --> 17:09.210
Let him shoot as he likes outside of it.

17:10.840 --> 17:13.840
Listen guys, do as we've planned.

17:13.840 --> 17:14.720
Yeah!

17:15.470 --> 17:16.510
All right!

17:16.510 --> 17:19.220
Go and enjoy football to your heart's content!

17:20.810 --> 17:22.230
The players are in the field!

17:22.850 --> 17:25.560
The last event of the
inter-school tournament is about to begin.

17:25.560 --> 17:29.440
The victor of the 26th inter-school tournament
will be decided after this match.

17:29.440 --> 17:31.360
Do your best, Tsubasa!

17:31.360 --> 17:32.490
This match is also the fated showdown

17:32.490 --> 17:36.490
between Tsubasa and Shuutetsu's Wakabayashi.

17:36.490 --> 17:38.120
Wakabayashi?

17:38.120 --> 17:40.410
See him? He's Shuutetsu's goalkeeper.

17:41.080 --> 17:43.870
Is that Wakabayashi?

17:43.870 --> 17:47.670
Both teams have spread out into the field.

17:47.670 --> 17:50.750
The champion of the national tournament,
Shuutetsu Elementary is as follows:

17:50.750 --> 17:54.760
Centre forwards are number 9,
Kisugi "the scorer" and number 11, Taki.

17:54.760 --> 17:56.630
There are four midfielders.

17:56.630 --> 18:00.100
Number 10 Izawa makes the
plays for Shuutetsu's attacks.

18:00.100 --> 18:05.770
In the defence, number 6, centre back
Takasugi is making his presence felt.

18:05.770 --> 18:09.360
The goal is trusted with
the genius goalkeeper Wakabayashi

18:09.360 --> 18:12.110
who has protected it without even conceding
a goal in the national tournament.

18:13.230 --> 18:16.360
It's about kick-off time.

18:18.200 --> 18:19.490
Ishizaki...

18:19.490 --> 18:21.490
You are the forward?

18:21.490 --> 18:22.540
You could say that.

18:22.540 --> 18:24.200
Isn't it that Oozora guy?

18:24.200 --> 18:25.460
You mean Tsubasa?

18:25.460 --> 18:27.540
Yeah, we thought he would be.

18:28.710 --> 18:31.040
If you want Tsubasa, he's over there.

18:31.710 --> 18:32.960
What?

18:34.710 --> 18:38.430
Captain, why is he in such a place?

18:38.430 --> 18:41.350
You told us to mark Oozora, but at this rate...

18:41.350 --> 18:43.350
He's in the centre-back!

18:43.350 --> 18:45.680
Is Tsubasa playing as a centre-back?

18:45.680 --> 18:47.520
I'm counting on you, Tsubasa!

18:47.520 --> 18:48.730
Leave it to me.

18:50.610 --> 18:51.940
What's going on?

18:51.940 --> 18:55.030
Tsubasa isn't a forward...

18:56.150 --> 18:58.280
I have no idea what you are trying to pull but

18:58.280 --> 18:59.410
I'm okay with it!

18:59.410 --> 19:01.870
We will be getting scores on your goal!

19:01.870 --> 19:04.240
Everyone! Go at it with all your might!

19:04.240 --> 19:05.450
Yeah!

19:07.580 --> 19:10.250
The referee has blown his whistle!

19:10.250 --> 19:13.670
With Shuutetsu's kick-off, the match has finally begun!

19:13.670 --> 19:15.090
Everyone, let's go!

19:15.090 --> 19:16.300
All right!

19:16.300 --> 19:16.970
Okay!

19:17.880 --> 19:18.590
Damn it!

19:19.840 --> 19:21.390
Nice!

19:23.890 --> 19:25.390
Kurata, pass it to me!

19:25.390 --> 19:26.810
Okay!

19:26.810 --> 19:28.730
God damn it!

19:28.730 --> 19:30.190
Shuutetsu is attacking.

19:30.190 --> 19:33.440
They are connecting complex passes
and steadily advancing to Nankatsu's side.

19:34.770 --> 19:37.860
The ball has returned to Izawa, the control tower.

19:37.860 --> 19:38.780
Let's go!

19:40.150 --> 19:44.120
With Izawa's signal, Shuutetsu's switch has turned on.

19:44.120 --> 19:45.370
Damn this guy!

19:47.580 --> 19:49.870
To Taki in the wing...

19:51.670 --> 19:53.670
This is a tactic Shuutetsu is known for!

19:53.670 --> 19:55.420
I'm leaving it to you, Sakurai!

19:56.170 --> 20:00.130
After dribbling, he crosses the ball before the goal line.

20:00.130 --> 20:02.050
Forward Kisugi is attacking.

20:02.050 --> 20:04.350
Shuutetsu's play pattern for certain victory.

20:04.350 --> 20:05.010
All right!

20:06.010 --> 20:08.270
Will Shuutetsu have the first goal?

20:10.100 --> 20:11.230
Cut!

20:11.230 --> 20:13.650
Nankatsu has just cut through that shot!

20:14.400 --> 20:15.020
What!

20:15.020 --> 20:16.230
You did it!

20:16.230 --> 20:18.440
Tsubasa for you!

20:21.070 --> 20:22.700
Tsubasa!

20:22.700 --> 20:25.120
I see now. So, that's how they utilized him.

20:25.120 --> 20:29.450
Shuutetsu's certain victory pattern is crumbled down.

20:29.450 --> 20:30.790
What are you doing?

20:30.790 --> 20:32.540
Hurry up and take the ball back!

20:32.540 --> 20:33.960
Sure!

20:37.670 --> 20:39.130
What?

20:39.130 --> 20:40.050
Bastard!

20:41.470 --> 20:42.760
A superb feint!

20:42.760 --> 20:45.600
Shuutetsu can't even touch the ball.

20:45.600 --> 20:47.850
Who's that guy?

20:47.850 --> 20:50.850
Did we have a guy like him
who could handle the ball so well?

20:51.850 --> 20:54.150
Didn't you know?

20:54.150 --> 20:58.530
He's the famous Oozora Tsubasa!

20:58.530 --> 21:00.440
Oozora Tsubasa...

21:00.440 --> 21:02.820
Hey, Tsubasa!

21:03.740 --> 21:05.740
Ishizaki!

21:05.740 --> 21:07.160
A long pass!

21:07.160 --> 21:09.410
The ball is in front of the goal in an instant.

21:09.410 --> 21:12.460
Tsubasa, why aren't you coming up here?

21:12.460 --> 21:15.580
This match is supposed
to be a contest between you and me.

21:15.580 --> 21:16.380
Oh no.

21:17.040 --> 21:18.920
I've got this pass!

21:18.920 --> 21:21.340
Why are you passing the ball to Ishizaki?

21:21.340 --> 21:23.840
I did it! No one's marking me.

21:23.840 --> 21:26.640
Ishizaki has entered the penalty area.

21:26.640 --> 21:28.890
Go, Nankatsu!

21:28.890 --> 21:31.890
Take this, Wakabayashi!

21:31.890 --> 21:33.690
Ishizaki has shot!

21:36.020 --> 21:37.060
Captain!

21:37.060 --> 21:39.610
Why are you not attacking me, Tsubasa?

21:42.820 --> 21:44.150
He stopped it.

21:44.150 --> 21:45.570
What?

21:45.570 --> 21:48.660
Shuutetsu's Wakabayashi, the best goalkeeper of the country,

21:48.660 --> 21:52.370
has stopped Nankatsu's shot without even budging.

21:53.040 --> 21:54.080
You guys!

21:54.080 --> 21:55.710
Our enemy is Tsubasa alone.

21:55.710 --> 21:57.210
Hurry up and score some goals.

21:57.210 --> 21:59.380
Our goal is to score 50 in this match.

22:00.500 --> 22:01.630
50 goals...

22:01.630 --> 22:02.920
Izawa!

22:05.170 --> 22:07.970
Tsubasa... Come and attack me.

22:07.970 --> 22:12.770
Wakabayashi, this too is a contest between you and me.

22:38.880 --> 22:44.760
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.880 --> 22:44.760
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.760 --> 22:50.760
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.760 --> 22:50.760
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.760 --> 22:56.770
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.760 --> 22:56.770
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.770 --> 23:02.150
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.770 --> 23:02.150
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:08.280
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:08.280
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:15.080
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.200 --> 23:15.080
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.290 --> 23:21.130
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.290 --> 23:26.130
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.330 --> 23:26.130
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.510 --> 23:33.260
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.510 --> 23:33.260
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.260 --> 23:39.190
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.480 --> 23:45.980
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.520 --> 23:45.980
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.700 --> 23:58.830
COMING UP, EPISODE 7:
TSUBASA THE FANTASISTA
